From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:28:30 -0700
Subject: soc: apple: rtkit: acknowledge the v2 PMP's CoreAnalytics events on
 any board

The empty CoreAnalytics event on the PMP's endpoint 7 is acknowledged
on the J714s only. It is the firmware's doing, not the board's: a
K116s's PMP sends it too, on the same endpoint. Acknowledge it for
every registry-v2 PMP.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
index 1276833aecc..0a329cf6cff 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
@@ -2408,8 +2408,7 @@ static struct apple_rtkit *__apple_rtkit_init(struct device *dev, void *cookie,
 		goto free_rtk;
 	rtk->pmp_registry_v2 =
 		of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-pmp-v2");
-	rtk->pmp_ca_event_ack = rtk->pmp_registry_v2 &&
-				of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s");
+	rtk->pmp_ca_event_ack = rtk->pmp_registry_v2;
 
 	init_completion(&rtk->epmap_completion);
 	init_completion(&rtk->coreanalytics_completion);
